1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,064
Pepsi put a fighter

2
00:00:01,064 --> 00:00:02,960
jet in a commercial.

3
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,771
Seven million Pepsi Points.

4
00:00:04,771 --> 00:00:06,659
Obviously a joke... right?

5
00:00:06,709 --> 00:00:07,953
Not to John Leonard.

6
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:09,218
In 1996,

7
00:00:09,218 --> 00:00:11,008
he spotted something in the rules.

8
00:00:11,008 --> 00:00:11,983
You could BUY

9
00:00:11,983 --> 00:00:13,436
extra Pepsi Points.

10
00:00:13,436 --> 00:00:14,696
For ten cents each.

11
00:00:14,696 --> 00:00:16,336
So he found investors.

12
00:00:16,336 --> 00:00:18,726
Collected fifteen real Pepsi Points.

13
00:00:18,726 --> 00:00:19,794
And mailed Pepsi a check

14
00:00:19,794 --> 00:00:21,743
for over seven hundred thousand dollars.

15
00:00:21,743 --> 00:00:23,423
His order form?

16
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:25,028
ONE HARRIER JET.

17
00:00:25,028 --> 00:00:26,619
Pepsi sent the check back.

18
00:00:26,619 --> 00:00:27,292
They said the jet

19
00:00:27,292 --> 00:00:28,598
wasn't a real prize.

20
00:00:28,598 --> 00:00:30,127
John took them to court.

21
00:00:30,127 --> 00:00:31,660
The judge sided with Pepsi.

22
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:33,065
No reasonable person would

23
00:00:33,065 --> 00:00:33,831
think the ad was

24
00:00:33,831 --> 00:00:35,444
offering a real fighter jet.

25
00:00:35,444 --> 00:00:36,889
John never got the plane.

26
00:00:36,889 --> 00:00:37,969
But he turned a soda

27
00:00:37,969 --> 00:00:40,681
commercial into a federal court case.
